<title>POLAND: Polish zloty fix stronger at 2.98 pct from parity.</title>
<headline>Polish zloty fix stronger at 2.98 pct from parity.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0455 to the dollar, up from 3.0555 yesterday and at 1.8065 against the mark, down from 1.8060, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 2.98 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Wednesday's 2.82 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
